# 1_200_000_000 + 1_200_000_000 = 2_400_000_000, over Natural'Last
# (2147483647). RopeTool.Mod's own Cat overflow guard HALTs(1) with no
# output (run-tests.sh's original strip() drops the Oberon runtime's
# "Terminated by Halt(1)." line); Ropes.New_Concat instead raises
# Ada.Strings.Length_Error, which rope_tool's bigcat handler catches
# and turns into a clean "Error: ..." message -- an exception, not a
# clamp, so this is one of the few fixtures where the *kind* of
# divergence (not just the wording) differs from the Oberon original.
program rope_tool
arg bigcat
arg 1200000000
arg x
arg 1200000000
arg y
status 1
output
Error: combined length exceeds Natural'Last
